  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\u03a0$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=\u27e82,0,2\u27e9+t\u27e83,2,-3\u27e9,\\,\u03a0:r\\cdot \u27e85,-2,3\u27e9=6.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=\u27e82+3t,2t,2-3t\u27e9.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e82+3t,2t,2-3t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e85,-2,3\u27e9 & =6 \\\\ \u27e82+3t,2t,2-3t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e85,-2,3\u27e9 & =6 \\\\ 5(2+3t)-2(2t)+3(2-3t) & =6 \\\\ 10+15t-4t+6-9t & =6 \\\\ 2t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e82+3(-5),2(-5),2-3(-5)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-13,-10,17\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-13,-10,17).$",
